  "id": "DrugBank_DB00620 - MONDO_grouped_19558_4706",
  "verbalization": "Triamcinolone, a corticosteroid, is linked to Discoid Lupus Erythematosus (DLE) through a chain of indications that all point to Prednicarbate as a common intermediate. The evidence suggests that Triamcinolone may be used in conditions such as Lichen Disease, Neurodermatitis, and Occupational Dermatitis, all of which are associated with DLE. This implies a potential mechanism where Triamcinolone, through its corticosteroid properties, may modulate inflammatory responses that are implicated in the development of DLE. The shared pathway involving Prednicarbate further supports the idea that Triamcinolone could be repurposed for DLE, given its ability to influence inflammatory processes. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, reinforcing the likelihood of a repurposing relationship, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
